  "result": "I fixed it, and subcommands now get their defaults from `default_map` again.\n\n**The bug:** In `src/click/core.py:392`, a subcommand's context was given the parent's entire `default_map`. It should only get the section stored under the subcommand's own name. So with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"from-map\"}}`, the `sub` command looked up `name` at the top level, didn't find it, and fell back to the option's normal default.\n\n**The fix:**\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)\n```\n\n**Tests:**\n- I added `test_default_map_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- The full test run passed: 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. Pytest also reported 31,000 tests as \"deselected\", so some tests are filtered out by the project's pytest setup and weren't run.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
